cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use solar-dynamics-observatory in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: solar-dynamics-observatory
abstract: >-
  solar-dynamics-observatory, imported as sdo, is a Python library for
  downloading and analyzing observations from NASA's Solar Dynamics
  Observatory (SDO). It searches the Joint Science Operations Center (JSOC)
  using sunpy and downloads filtergrams from the Atmospheric Imaging Assembly
  (AIA) and magnetograms from the Helioseismic and Magnetic Imager (HMI),
  caching the results so that repeated requests are served from disk. AIA
  images can be prepared for scientific analysis with aiapy, which rotates
  each image to solar north up and scales it to a common plate scale. Rather
  than sunpy maps, observations are represented as named-arrays function
  arrays, so a sequence of images has named axes and physical units, and
  carries the time, wavelength, and sky position of every pixel.
